Z||000000||PAUL88GT||10-17-2000||01:25 PM||||My 88gt did not have drip rails or rain gutters when I purchased it.  Are they needed? Where can I purchase them? Are they easy to install?<P>TIA<BR>Paul||||reg||5
Z||000001||1FST2M6||10-17-2000||02:36 PM||||yeah.. same qusetion! i pulled mine off to paint the car.. and don't like them on... will bad things happen to my family if i leave them off?<P>------------------<BR>Shhh.. Top Secret! <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/1fstcheeto_2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||rockcrawl||10-17-2000||03:17 PM||||I left them off when I rebuilt an 87 GT, and I had no problems with it. The only thing that might be a problem is driving in the rain with the window open, more water is likely to get inside.<P>------------------<BR>Jon Lagler<BR>'87 GT (awaiting new engine)<BR>4.9 liter V8 Testarossa Spyder (under construction)<P>"Confidence is the feeling you have before you fully understand the situation"||||reg||1
Z||000003||WisconsinGT||10-17-2000||03:26 PM||||No they are not needed. (I don"t think Fieros  The are very hard to find. But I know there are several around. Yes, they are very easy to install. Good luck!||||reg||1
Z||000004||Tigger||10-17-2000||04:13 PM||||I had one that was karate choped pretty good. Never had the thought about putting them back on, I like the look without them.<P>They are just pressed on and easy to install.  You could probably find and pull them off a Fiero in the boneyard.<P>Without them, if you've got beaded water on the roof you will get a few drops on you when you get in.  Small price to pay I guess.  Driving in the rain you won't want to crack the window no more than 1/2" but why would you want them down in the rain anyway?<P>Here's a picture of what mine looks like without them.<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/tiggerside.gif"> <p>[This message has been edited by Tigger (edited 10-17-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||Monkeyman||10-17-2000||09:45 PM||||Some of us smokers would like the window cracked even in the rain.  I like the look without them, but mine have to stay.||||reg||1
Z||000006||stsmithgt||10-18-2000||01:41 PM||||Hey! I drive with my head out the window in the rain! woof woof! J/K||||reg||6
Z||000007||ThatRickGuy||10-18-2000||02:45 PM||||I think the previous owner of mine removed them, but being a smoker, I am interested in them. Do they really look that bad?||||reg||1
Z||000008||Standard||10-19-2000||02:09 AM||||I was going to pull them off my GT today, but when I saw all the crud that had built up under them I decided to leave them on... ugh.  I can't wait 'till I have some money for a paint job...<P>------------------<BR>Mike -<BR>Black 86.5 GT 5 Spd, 151,000 miles and counting!         <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/BURNOUT.gif">      <BR>Red 84 Sport Coupe - winter donut maker   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/asthanos.gif"> ||||reg||1
